"""
Metadata Aggregator

Reads the YAML front matter (and the %% definitions %% blocks) of every page in
the vault, resolves the definition keys, normalises dates, and writes one
database that the other programs read:

    Meta/Programs/debug/metadata_aggregator/extracted_metadata.json

While it does that it checks the metadata against the rules in Meta/Metadata.md
and writes a report of everything that looks wrong:

    Meta/Programs/debug/metadata_aggregator/metadata_warnings.txt

Issues come in three levels:
    error   - something is broken: a program will produce wrong or missing output.
    warning - very likely a mistake.
    notice  - style or consistency; worth a look, safe to ignore.

The allowed tags, types, statuses, futures and has/needs values are read from
Meta/Metadata.md itself, so documenting a new tag there is all it takes for the
checker to accept it.

Usage:
    python metadata_aggregator.py              # write the JSON and the report
    python metadata_aggregator.py --dry-run    # print the report, write nothing
    python metadata_aggregator.py --strict     # exit with code 1 if there are errors
    python metadata_aggregator.py --quiet      # leave notices out of the console output

Status: pages of the types in mysenvar_common.STATUS_TYPES carry a block

    status:
      scope: standard      # brief, standard, overview or generated
      progress: wip        # empty, idea, wip, stub or complete
      future: [pending]    # any of pending, rewrite, review (or [])

Subpages: a subpage without `type`, or without `status` (or any of its three
keys), takes its parent page's value. This isn't reported.
"""
